From af05cd27ec73f751f6f406c910ac84021e587041 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 13:45:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] VAX: Add DMF32 multi-function communications interface
 (Unibus VAXen)

Standalone variant: applies to Open SIMH 87eb7d5 without the DMV11/DMP11
commit (use it instead of that commit and the normal DMF32 commit).
All four functions: synchronous interface, 8-line asynchronous
multiplexer, line printer controller and DR11-C compatible parallel
interface.

The units are named after their function: DMF-ASYNC (multiplexer),
DMF-PRINT (line printer), DMF-SYNC (synchronous line) and DMF-PAR
(parallel interface user device); DMF0-DMF4 are accepted as well, and the
internal timer unit DMF2 is not shown.  The synchronous line's peer is set
with SET DMF-SYNC PEER= or SET DMF PEER=.

The synchronous line and the parallel interface are polled once per
clock tick (like the asynchronous lines and the DMC11), so SET CPU IDLE
works while DMF-SYNC or DMF-PAR is attached.

SHOW DMF-SYNC and SHOW DMF-PAR report their own line
(connected/disconnected), not the asynchronous lines.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
