+
+   dmf          DMF32 (M8396) - synchronous line, asynchronous multiplexer,
+                line printer and parallel interface
+
+   References:
+     EK-DMF32-UG-003  DMF32 User's Guide (programming, chapter 4)
+     EK-DMF32-TD-001  DMF32 Multi-Function Communications Interface
+                      Technical Description (CSR map, CSR0/CSR1, vectors)
+
+   The DMF32 is a single Unibus module for VAX systems that combines four
+   independently programmed devices behind one block of 16 registers:
+
+     base+00  COMBO CSR0      device code (15:12), first vector/4 (7:0)
+     base+02  COMBO CSR1      diagnostic register; LP maintenance data (7:0)
+     base+04  SYNC  RCSR      synchronous receive CSR
+     base+06  SYNC  TCSR      synchronous transmit CSR
+     base+10  SYNC  MISC      indirect address, master reset; data set change flags
+     base+12  SYNC  IND       indirect registers selected by MISC (3:0)
+     base+14  ASYNC CSR       8-line asynchronous multiplexer
+     base+16  ASYNC LPR       line parameter register
+     base+20  ASYNC RBUF/RSP  receive silo (read) / silo alarm timeout (write)
+     base+22  ASYNC IND       indirect registers selected by CSR (4:0)
+     base+24  LP    CSR       LP32 line printer controller
+     base+26  LP    IND       indirect registers selected by LP CSR (10:8)
+     base+30  DR    CSR       parallel interface CSR
+     base+32  DR    OUTBUF    output buffer
+     base+34  DR    INBUF     input buffer (read) / miscellaneous (write)
+     base+36  DR    IND       indirect registers selected by CSR (4:3)
+
+   Eight interrupt vectors follow the base vector loaded into CSR0:
+     +0 sync receive, +4 sync transmit, +10 parallel A, +14 parallel B,
+     +20 async receive, +24 async transmit, +30 line printer, +34 unused.
+
+   All four functions are emulated.  As on the module, the line printer
+   and the parallel interface share one connector and one set of hardware,
+   so a DMF32 has one or the other: SET DMF CONFIG= sets distribution panel
+   switch pack 3 (PRINTER = async, sync and line printer, device code 1110,
+   the default; PARALLEL = async, sync and parallel interface, 1101; ASYNCLP
+   = 1010; ASYNC = 1000).  Functions not configured do not respond.
+
+   Units (their names, set in dmf_reset; DMFn also works):
+     DMF-ASYNC  (DMF0)  asynchronous multiplexer, lines 0-7
+     DMF-PRINT  (DMF1)  line printer output file
+                (DMF2)  silo alarm timer, internal and not shown
+     DMF-SYNC   (DMF3)  synchronous line
+     DMF-PAR    (DMF4)  parallel interface user device
+
+   Synchronous interface (User's Guide 4.2 - 4.6)
+     - One line (unit DMF-SYNC) over TCP to a peer: another DMF32, or any of the
+       DMC11/DMR11/DMP11/DMV11 emulations, since in DDCMP mode the line
+       carries standard DDCMP frames.
+     - Double-buffered DMA transmit and receive (primary/secondary buffer
+       address and count registers) with the done, error and
+       primary/secondary bits of the receive and transmit CSRs.
+     - DDCMP (CRC generation and checking, message length from the header,
+       tributary address check), HDLC/SDLC (FCS, secondary address check)
+       and GEN BYTE (raw characters, sync detection, strip sync, match
+       character) framing; internal loop; modem status follows the
+       connection, with data set change interrupts.
+
+   Asynchronous multiplexer (User's Guide 4.7 - 4.10)
+     - 8 lines on a terminal multiplexer (Telnet or serial ports); lines 0
+       and 1 have modem control (with ATTACH -M).
+     - Output from a 32 character silo per line, or by DMA from memory
+       (buffer address and count in indirect registers 16-31), with the
+       preempt character and auto XON/XOFF.
+     - Input into one 48 entry receive silo with line numbers, error flags
+       and data set change entries; interrupt after more than 16 entries or
+       when the silo alarm timeout (RSP) expires.
+     - Maintenance modes: auto echo, local loopback, remote loopback.
+
+   Parallel interface (User's Guide 4.14 - 4.16)
+     - DR11-C functional mode, 32-word silo modes and double-buffered DMA
+       modes; the user device is connected to unit DMF-PAR (TCP or a serial
+       port) and exchanges the interface signals as short text messages
+       (see the parallel interface section below).
+
+   Line printer controller (User's Guide 4.11 - 4.13)
+     - DMA output of one buffer per print cycle to the attached file, with
+       prefix and suffix characters and the optional formatting functions
+       (carriage return insertion, form feed to line feeds, tab expansion,
+       line wrap or truncation, lower to upper case, non printable filter).
+     - Status words bytes transmitted and line count; maintenance mode
+       loops data into CSR1 (7:0).
+*/
+
+#if !defined (VM_VAX)
+#error "DMF32 is only supported on Unibus VAX systems"
+#endif
